Onboarding
Implement digital patient forms
Patient can open digital intake forms.
 Patient can enter required information.
 Required fields prevent incomplete submission.
 Patient can submit the completed form.
 Submitted information is saved to the patient's record.
 A confirmation message appears after submission.
As a patient, I want to be able to do my forms digitally before arriving at the clinic to ensure that it’s saved on my record.

Build a medical history questionnaire 
Questionnaire contains required medical-history fields.
 Patient can save and complete the questionnaire.
 Required questions must be completed before submission.
 Submitted answers are stored with the patient profile.
 Patient receives confirmation after submission.
	As a patient I would like to complete a questionnaire to have my medical history on file so that I can be properly acquitted.

Upload patient documents
Patient can select a document from their device.
 System accepts supported file types.
 System rejects unsupported file types.
 Uploaded documents are associated with the correct patient.
 Patient receives confirmation that the document was uploaded.
	As a patient I would like to be able to upload personal documents and get document confirmation once uploaded.

Digital consent forms
Patient can view the consent form.
 Patient can provide a digital signature.
 System records the date and time of consent.
 Patient cannot submit without completing required consent fields.
 Completed consent is stored with the patient record.
As a patient I want digital consent forms that I can view and sign with the date and time after completing the consent fields.

	Appointment Scheduling
Scheduling interface
Patient can view available appointment dates.
 Patient can view available appointment times.
 Patient can select an available appointment.
 System prevents double-booking.
 Appointment is added to the patient's account.
 Patient receives a scheduling confirmation.

As a patient I want to be able to view my appointment dates, times, and be able to select an available appointment without being able to double book.

Text/Email Reminders
Patient can provide or update contact information.
 System sends a reminder before the appointment.
 Reminder contains the appointment date and time.
 Patient can select text, email, or both when supported.
 Reminder delivery is recorded by the system.
	As a patient I want to be able to update contact information and have reminders making sure I’m able to get to my appointment on time. 

Automated Systems
AI Call System
System can receive incoming calls.
 System can identify common patient questions.
 System provides predefined responses.
 System can transfer the caller to staff when necessary.
 Failed or transferred calls are recorded.
As a patient I want an automated voice system that can identify and answer my questions and transfer my call when needed.

Automated Billing
System generates a bill from the appropriate patient account.
 Bill includes the amount owed.
 Bill includes relevant service information.
 Patient can view the bill electronically.
 Billing status is updated after payment or adjustment.
	As a patient I would like to be opted into automated billing system that records the amount owed and the service information that can be viewed and updated.
  
Verification
Insurance and ID
Employee can view verification status.
 Insurance and ID status are displayed separately.
 Status indicates whether verification is complete.
 Missing information is clearly identified.
 Only authorized employees can view verification information.
	As an employee I want to be able to view my verification status displaying my insurance and ID status only able to viewed by authorized employees. 
	Patient Profile
  
Management Page
Patient can access their management page.
 Patient can view their personal information.
 Patient can update permitted information.
 Changes are saved successfully.
As a patient I want to be able to access my management page to view my personal information that I can update if needed. 
 Patient receives confirmation after updating information.
 
Authentication
Patient can create an account.
 Patient can log in with valid credentials.
 Invalid credentials are rejected.
 Passwords are handled securely.
 Patient can log out.
 Protected information cannot be accessed without authentication.
	As a patient I want to be able to create an account with my valid credentials and passwords being handled securely that cannot be accessed without proper authentication.

  
